        "original_id": "792a07e1-fa87-55bc-8e92-dfc725507c81",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Toyota Owners 400, Federated Auto Parts 400, Daytona Speedweeks\n- Companies: Crown Royal, Diageo, Seagram\n- Organizations: Monster Energy NASCAR Cup Series\n- Places: Richmond Raceway, Richmond, Virginia\n- Concepts: race title sponsorship, essay contest\n\nFacts:\n- In 2000, Diageo purchased Crown Royal when the Seagram portfolio was dissolved.\n- Crown Royal is a blended Canadian whisky.\n- From 2007 to 2011, Crown Royal was the former title sponsor of the Toyota Owners 400.\n- From 2007 to 2011, Crown Royal named the Toyota Owners 400 after the winner of an essay contest during Daytona Speedweeks.\n- The Federated Auto Parts 400 is an annual Monster Energy NASCAR Cup Series stock car race held at Richmond Raceway in Richmond, Virginia.\n- The Federated Auto Parts 400 is the second of two Richmond Raceway races, with the Toyota Owners 400 held there in the spring as the first race.",
